e head to dominate at around 40% of the frame with its glowing brain, the growth graphic as a secondary connector at 25%, and the book smaller at 20%, keeping strictly to the two-to-three element rule with one clear focal point, and I'm working through the color harmony — the cream and gold both sit in the warm family, so intensifying the glow should let it read as dominant without clashing.\n\nThat makes sense — the growth visually leads into the head. Now I'm refining the palette for harmony: gold-toned translucent growth blocks instead of multicolor, a warm dark brown silhouette instead of pure black, and a layered orange-to-gold gradient for the brain glow, plus a subtle vignette on the cream background to frame everything.\n\nI'm thinking through opacity levels next — growth blocks at 70-80% so they blend into the background while the head and book stay fully opaque, and I want the blocks to gain a soft glow as they get bigger, culminating in the brain's full glow. For text, minimal or none, since the book cover already shows the title — maybe just a small audiobook label at the bottom. The real idea forming is that the growth curve should act as a visual bridge, letting knowledge flow from the book through the blocks into the mind.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872304104.png","toolAction":"Examining generated thumbnail","toolSummary":"Lit Mind result"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872326940.png","toolAction":"Examining generated thumbnail","toolSummary":"Stacking Micro result"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2b145ed9-35fe-4974-bd1c-54311bc3cd9c/.user_uploaded/media_1789872340889.png","toolAction":"Examining generated thumbnail","toolSummary":"Broken Chain resu